---
/**
 * Architecture of TabulaView.ai, drawn from the repo's docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/AGENT_WORKFLOW.md.
 * Colours come from the design tokens (CSS variables), so the diagram follows the palette.
 */
---

<figure class="not-prose my-10">
  {/* eslint-disable astro/jsx-a11y/no-noninteractive-tabindex -- scrollable on phones, must be keyboard-reachable */}
  <div
    class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-line bg-cream-soft p-4 sm:p-6"
    tabindex="0"
    role="region"
    aria-label="Architecture diagram (scrolls sideways on small screens)"
  >
    {/* eslint-enable astro/jsx-a11y/no-noninteractive-tabindex */}
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 760 470"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="tv-arch-title tv-arch-desc"
      class="h-auto w-full min-w-[34rem] font-sans"
    >
      <title id="tv-arch-title">TabulaView.ai architecture</title>
      <desc id="tv-arch-desc">
        The browser keeps the file and sends it with each request to a stateless FastAPI backend. Python ingests,
        profiles and analyses the data and runs 13 statistical tools whose results are stored as evidence. An LLM, Groq
        first then NVIDIA, or a rules-based analyst if both fail, chooses tools and words findings. A grounding check
        compares every number in a finding with its evidence; unmatched findings are sent back for correction, then
        flagged unverified if they still fail. A scorecard compares the AI and rules-based analyses and the higher score
        builds the dashboard and PDF or PowerPoint report. Supabase stores accounts and aggregated reports only, never
        rows.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker
          id="tv-arrow"
          viewBox="0 0 10 10"
          refX="9"
          refY="5"
          markerWidth="7"
          markerHeight="7"
          orient="auto-start-reverse"
        >
          <path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" fill="var(--color-forest)"></path>
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <style>
        .box {
          fill: var(--color-cream);
          stroke: var(--color-forest);
          stroke-width: 1.5;
        }
        .key {
          fill: var(--color-cream);
          stroke: var(--color-pink);
          stroke-width: 3;
        }
        .zone {
          fill: none;
          stroke: var(--color-line);
          stroke-width: 1.5;
          stroke-dasharray: 6 5;
        }
        .t {
          fill: var(--color-forest);
          font-size: 15px;
          font-weight: 600;
        }
        .s {
          fill: var(--color-forest-muted);
          font-size: 12.5px;
        }
        .z {
          fill: var(--color-forest-muted);
          font-size: 12px;
          font-weight: 600;
          letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        }
        .a {
          stroke: var(--color-forest);
          stroke-width: 1.5;
          fill: none;
          marker-end: url(#tv-arrow);
        }
      </style>

      <!-- Browser -->
      <rect class="box" x="10" y="40" width="160" height="96" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="24" y="66">
        Browser
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="24" y="88">
        React + TypeScript
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="24" y="106">
        keeps the file in
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="24" y="122">
        memory, re-sends it
      </text>

      <!-- Backend zone -->
      <rect class="zone" x="210" y="14" width="540" height="300" rx="14"></rect>
      <text class="z" x="226" y="36">
        FASTAPI · STATELESS, NOTHING STORED
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="226" y="50" width="150" height="70" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="240" y="76">
        Ingest + profile
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="240" y="98">
        types, missing, invalid,
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="240" y="113">
        duplicates
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="400" y="50" width="150" height="70" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="414" y="76">
        13 stat tools
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="414" y="98">
        results saved as
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="414" y="113">
        evidence E1, E2 …
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="574" y="50" width="160" height="70" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="588" y="76">
        LLM analyst
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="588" y="98">
        Groq → NVIDIA,
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="588" y="113">
        or rules if both fail
      </text>

      <rect class="key" x="574" y="150" width="160" height="78" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="588" y="176">
        Grounding check
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="588" y="197">
        every number must be
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="588" y="212">
        in its cited evidence
      </text>

      <rect class="key" x="400" y="150" width="150" height="78" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="414" y="176">
        Scorecard
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="414" y="197">
        AI vs rules-based,
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="414" y="212">
        higher score wins
      </text>

      <rect class="box" x="226" y="150" width="150" height="78" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="240" y="176">
        Dashboard
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="240" y="197">
        + PDF / PowerPoint
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="240" y="212">
        report
      </text>

      <text class="s" x="590" y="262">
        fails → sent back to fix,
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="590" y="278">
        then flagged “unverified”
      </text>

      <!-- Supabase -->
      <rect class="box" x="226" y="360" width="300" height="84" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="240" y="388">
        Supabase (optional accounts)
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="240" y="410">
        Google / GitHub sign-in · Postgres RLS
      </text>
      <text class="s" x="240" y="427">
        saves aggregated reports only, never rows
      </text>

      <!-- Arrows -->
      <path class="a" d="M170 88 H222"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M376 85 H396"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M550 85 H570"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M654 120 V146"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M574 189 H554"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M400 189 H380"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M654 228 V246"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M300 228 V356"></path>
      <path class="a" d="M226 189 H120 V140"></path>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-forest-muted">
    Python computes every number; the LLM only chooses which tools to run and words the findings. Drawn from the repo's
    <code>ARCHITECTURE.md</code> and <code>AGENT_WORKFLOW.md</code>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
